WEBVTT

00:00:21.783 --> 00:00:22.951
-NEWT: Step back.
-(GASPS)

00:00:24.035 --> 00:00:25.245
Step back.

00:00:25.412 --> 00:00:26.705
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:00:26.872 --> 00:00:29.166
-What's the matter with this?
-I said, step away.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.460
What the hell is this thing?

00:00:33.211 --> 00:00:34.880
It's an Obscurus.

00:00:35.797 --> 00:00:37.299
I need to get going.

00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:39.968
Find everyone who's escaped,
before they get hurt.

00:00:40.135 --> 00:00:41.303
Before they get hurt?

00:00:41.469 --> 00:00:42.554
Yes, Mr. Kowalski.

00:00:42.721 --> 00:00:44.514
So they're currently in alien terrain

00:00:44.681 --> 00:00:47.726
surrounded by millions of the most
vicious creatures on the planet.

00:00:50.061 --> 00:00:51.396
Humans.

00:00:53.064 --> 00:00:56.526
So where would you say
that a medium-sized creature

00:00:56.693 --> 00:00:58.403
who likes broad open plains,

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.405
trees, sort of waterholes,
that sort of thing.

00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:01.907
Where might she go?

00:01:02.073 --> 00:01:03.241
In New York City?

00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:05.577
-Yes.
-Plains? (CHUCKLES)

00:01:06.786 --> 00:01:07.871
Central Park.

00:01:08.246 --> 00:01:09.623
And where is that exactly?

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:11.082
Where is Central Park?

00:01:15.587 --> 00:01:17.255
Well, look...

00:01:17.422 --> 00:01:18.590
I would come and show you,

00:01:18.757 --> 00:01:20.592
but don't you think it's kind
of a double-cross?

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:23.637
The girls take us in,
they make us hot cocoa--

00:01:23.803 --> 00:01:24.930
Now you do realize that once they see

00:01:25.096 --> 00:01:27.265
that you stopped sweating,
they will Obliviate you in a heartbeat?

00:01:27.432 --> 00:01:28.642
What's "Bliviate" mean?

00:01:28.808 --> 00:01:31.353
It'll be like you wake up
and all memory of magic gone.

00:01:36.024 --> 00:01:37.067
(STAMMERS) I won't remember any of this?

00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:39.027
No.

00:01:40.028 --> 00:01:41.029
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

00:01:43.281 --> 00:01:45.659
All right, yeah, okay. I'll help you.

00:01:50.455 --> 00:01:51.623
Come on, then.

00:02:09.766 --> 00:02:11.977
Credence, where have you been?

00:02:14.729 --> 00:02:17.691
I was looking for a place
for tomorrow's meeting.

00:02:20.151 --> 00:02:22.862
There's a corner
on 32nd Street that could--

00:02:30.954 --> 00:02:31.997
I'm sorry, Ma.

00:02:32.205 --> 00:02:33.915
I didn't realize it was so late.

00:03:02.861 --> 00:03:03.862
(RUMBLING)

00:03:07.657 --> 00:03:09.034
(RUMBLING CONTINUES)

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.597
-I was watching you at dinner.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.431 --> 00:03:33.391
People like you, don't they, Mr. Kowalski?

00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:35.018
Oh.

00:03:35.769 --> 00:03:38.063
Well, I'm sure people like you, too, huh?

00:03:38.229 --> 00:03:40.398
Not really, no. I annoy people.

00:03:42.025 --> 00:03:43.026
Ah.

00:03:43.693 --> 00:03:45.403
Why did you decide to be a baker?

00:03:46.071 --> 00:03:47.072
Well, um...

00:03:47.405 --> 00:03:48.656
Because I'm dying

00:03:48.823 --> 00:03:50.492
in that canning factory.

00:03:50.742 --> 00:03:54.079
Everyone there's dying.
It just crushes the life out of you.

00:03:54.371 --> 00:03:56.164
-Do you like canned food?
-No.

00:03:56.331 --> 00:03:57.957
Yeah, me neither.

00:03:58.249 --> 00:04:00.877
That's why I wanna make pastries.
You know, it makes people happy.

00:04:01.044 --> 00:04:02.379
We're going this way.

00:04:03.046 --> 00:04:04.422
So did you get your loan?

00:04:05.382 --> 00:04:06.466
No. (SCOFFS)

00:04:06.925 --> 00:04:08.301
I ain't got no collateral.

00:04:08.468 --> 00:04:10.595
Stayed in the army too long, apparently.
I don't know.

00:04:10.762 --> 00:04:12.222
You fought in the war?

00:04:12.389 --> 00:04:14.349
Of course I fought in the war.
Everyone fought in the war.

00:04:14.516 --> 00:04:17.102
-You didn't fight in the war?
-I worked mostly with dragons.

00:04:17.268 --> 00:04:18.436
Ukrainian Ironbellies.

00:04:18.853 --> 00:04:20.271
Eastern Front.

00:04:30.824 --> 00:04:32.117
(SOFT CLINKING)

00:04:44.045 --> 00:04:45.296
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:04:45.463 --> 00:04:46.506
(GROWLING)

00:04:49.551 --> 00:04:51.010
Fenestra.

00:04:52.303 --> 00:04:53.304
Oh!

00:04:58.935 --> 00:04:59.936
(CHITTERING)

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.744
(CRASHING)

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.956
-(NEWT YELPS)
-(CHANDELIER SHATTERING)

00:05:24.085 --> 00:05:26.171
(CREATURE ROARING)

00:05:35.847 --> 00:05:36.848
(EXHALES)

00:05:37.015 --> 00:05:38.433
(CREATURE GROWLING)

00:05:41.394 --> 00:05:43.021
(GLASS CRACKING)

00:05:46.274 --> 00:05:47.275
(CREATURE ROARING)

00:05:51.696 --> 00:05:53.031
-(CHITTERING)
-(GRUNTS)

00:05:53.531 --> 00:05:55.033
Accio.

